<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Math Supplement</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3.2 Optimal Reasoning Length Derivation ‣ 3 SmartThinker Design ‣ SmartThinker: Progressive Chain-of-Thought Length Calibration for Efficient Large Language Model Reasoning" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem 3.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide the detailed proof process of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3.2 Optimal Reasoning Length Derivation ‣ 3 SmartThinker Design ‣ SmartThinker: Progressive Chain-of-Thought Length Calibration for Efficient Large Language Model Reasoning" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem 3.1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="503.39" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 503.39" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,503.39) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#04A5E5;" fill="#04A5E5" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 497.48 C 0 500.74 2.64 503.39 5.91 503.39 L 471.47 503.39 C 474.73 503.39 477.38 500.74 477.38 497.48 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E6F6FC;" fill="#E6F6FC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 479.12 L 475.41 479.12 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#04A5E5;--ltx-fill-color:#04A5E5;--ltx-fg-color:#04A5E5;" color="#04A5E5" fill="#04A5E5" stroke="#04A5E5" stroke-dasharray="2.84528pt,2.84528pt" stroke-dashoffset="1.42264pt" stroke-opacity="1.0"><path style="fill:none" d="M 1.97 372.75 L 475.41 372.75"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 487.79)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.7em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.45" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.69)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3.2 Optimal Reasoning Length Derivation ‣ 3 SmartThinker Design ‣ SmartThinker: Progressive Chain-of-Thought Length Calibration for Efficient Large Language Model Reasoning" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#EFF1F5;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem 3.1</span></a></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 391.28)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:5.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.49em;font-size:10pt;" height="82.75" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 76.03)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> be the parameter of the current policy, <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> be the input prompt. Assume that the distribution of <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(l\mid q;\theta)\sim N(\mu_{1},\sigma_{1}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∼</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(l\mid q;\theta)\sim N(\mu_{1},\sigma_{1}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and the distribution of <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> given the correct reasoning condition is <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(l\mid r^{acc}=1,q;\theta\right)\sim N(\mu_{2},\sigma_{2}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∼</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(l\mid r^{acc}=1,q;\theta\right)\sim N(\mu_{2},\sigma_{2}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\left(r^{acc}=1\mid l;\theta\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\left(r^{acc}=1\mid l;\theta\right)</annotation></semantics></math> has a unique maximum <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iff\sigma_{1}^{2}&gt;\sigma_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iff\sigma_{1}^{2}&gt;\sigma_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the point is <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\arg\max\limits_{l}\Pr\left(r^{acc}=1\mid l;\theta\right)=\frac{\sigma_{1}^{2}\mu_{2}-\sigma_{2}^{2}\mu_{1}}{\sigma_{1}^{2}-\sigma_{2}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\arg\max\limits_{l}\Pr\left(r^{acc}=1\mid l;\theta\right)=\frac{\sigma_{1}^{2}\mu_{2}-\sigma_{2}^{2}\mu_{1}}{\sigma_{1}^{2}-\sigma_{2}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:24.89em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="347.16" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 344.47)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.3" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.3.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proof.</h6>
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">By Bayes’ theorem, the posterior probability of correct reasoning given the length <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> is expressed as:</span></span>
<span id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(r^{acc}=1\mid l,q;\theta)=\frac{p(l\mid r^{acc}=1,q;\theta)\Pr(r^{acc}=1\mid q;\theta)}{p(l\mid q;\theta)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(r^{acc}=1\mid l,q;\theta)=\frac{p(l\mid r^{acc}=1,q;\theta)\Pr(r^{acc}=1\mid q;\theta)}{p(l\mid q;\theta)}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Since <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(r^{acc}=1\mid\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(r^{acc}=1\mid\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimization objective satisfies:</span></span>
<span id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\arg\max_{l}\Pr(r^{acc}=1\mid l,q;\theta)=\arg\max_{l}\frac{p(l\mid r^{acc}=1,q;\theta)}{p(l\mid q;\theta)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\arg\max_{l}\Pr(r^{acc}=1\mid l,q;\theta)=\arg\max_{l}\frac{p(l\mid r^{acc}=1,q;\theta)}{p(l\mid q;\theta)}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Substituting the probability density functions for <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(\mu_{2},\sigma_{2}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(\mu_{2},\sigma_{2}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(\mu_{1},\sigma_{1}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(\mu_{1},\sigma_{1}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain:</span></span>
<span id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{p(l\mid r^{acc}=1,q;\theta)}{p(l\mid q;\theta)}=\frac{\sigma_{1}}{\sigma_{2}}\exp\left(\frac{(l-\mu_{1})^{2}}{2\sigma_{1}^{2}}-\frac{(l-\mu_{2})^{2}}{2\sigma_{2}^{2}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{p(l\mid r^{acc}=1,q;\theta)}{p(l\mid q;\theta)}=\frac{\sigma_{1}}{\sigma_{2}}\exp\left(\frac{(l-\mu_{1})^{2}}{2\sigma_{1}^{2}}-\frac{(l-\mu_{2})^{2}}{2\sigma_{2}^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Taking the natural logarithm and omitting terms constant with respect to <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the objective function:</span></span>
<span id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(l)=\frac{(l-\mu_{1})^{2}}{2\sigma_{1}^{2}}-\frac{(l-\mu_{2})^{2}}{2\sigma_{2}^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(l)=\frac{(l-\mu_{1})^{2}}{2\sigma_{1}^{2}}-\frac{(l-\mu_{2})^{2}}{2\sigma_{2}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The first-order condition for the maximum is <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{df}{dl}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{df}{dl}=0</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{l-\mu_{1}}{\sigma_{1}^{2}}-\frac{l-\mu_{2}}{\sigma_{2}^{2}}=0\implies(l-\mu_{1})\sigma_{2}^{2}=(l-\mu_{2})\sigma_{1}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{l-\mu_{1}}{\sigma_{1}^{2}}-\frac{l-\mu_{2}}{\sigma_{2}^{2}}=0\implies(l-\mu_{1})\sigma_{2}^{2}=(l-\mu_{2})\sigma_{1}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Solving for <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> yields the critical point:</span></span>
<span id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\text{opt}}=\frac{\sigma_{1}^{2}\mu_{2}-\sigma_{2}^{2}\mu_{1}}{\sigma_{1}^{2}-\sigma_{2}^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">opt</mtext></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\text{opt}}=\frac{\sigma_{1}^{2}\mu_{2}-\sigma_{2}^{2}\mu_{1}}{\sigma_{1}^{2}-\sigma_{2}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To confirm this is a maximum, we examine the second derivative:</span></span>
<span id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d^{2}f}{dl^{2}}=\frac{1}{\sigma_{1}^{2}}-\frac{1}{\sigma_{2}^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d^{2}f}{dl^{2}}=\frac{1}{\sigma_{1}^{2}}-\frac{1}{\sigma_{2}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">If and only if <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}^{2}&gt;\sigma_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}^{2}&gt;\sigma_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d^{2}f}{dl^{2}}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d^{2}f}{dl^{2}}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, which ensures that <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\text{opt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">opt</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\text{opt}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a global maximum.
∎</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>In-depth Analysis of the Optimal Length <math id="A1.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\text{opt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>l</mi><mtext>opt</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\text{opt}}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To better understand the properties of the proposed optimal reasoning length <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\text{opt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>l</mi><mtext>opt</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\text{opt}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we analyze the log-conditional-probability <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(l)=\ln\Pr(r^{\text{acc}}=1\mid l)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mtext>acc</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(l)=\ln\Pr(r^{\text{acc}}=1\mid l)</annotation></semantics></math>. According to Bayes’ theorem, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(r^{\text{acc}}=1\mid l)=\frac{\Pr(l\mid r^{\text{acc}}=1)\Pr(r^{\text{acc}}=1)}{\Pr(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mtext>acc</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mtext>acc</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mtext>acc</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(r^{\text{acc}}=1\mid l)=\frac{\Pr(l\mid r^{\text{acc}}=1)\Pr(r^{\text{acc}}=1)}{\Pr(l)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Maximizing this probability with respect to <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to maximizing the log-density ratio <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(l)=\ln\frac{p_{2}(l)}{p_{1}(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(l)=\ln\frac{p_{2}(l)}{p_{1}(l)}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1},p_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1},p_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are the probability density functions of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(\mu_{1},\sigma_{1}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(\mu_{1},\sigma_{1}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(\mu_{2},\sigma_{2}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(\mu_{2},\sigma_{2}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. <a href="#A1.F5" title='Figure 5 ‣ A.2 In-depth Analysis of the Optimal Length 𝑙^"opt" ‣ Appendix A Math Supplement ‣ SmartThinker: Progressive Chain-of-Thought Length Calibration for Efficient Large Language Model Reasoning' class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure 5</span></a> simply illustrates how the curve of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(l)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(l)</annotation></semantics></math> changes under different conditions.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F5" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2603.08000v1/opt_len.svg" id="A1.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/96;" width="476" height="96"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="A1.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The curve of <math id="A1.F5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(l)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(l)</annotation></semantics></math> under different conditions.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Curvature and Stability.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The second derivative of the objective function is:</p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial^{2}}{\partial l^{2}}\ln\frac{p_{2}(l)}{p_{1}(l)}=\frac{1}{\sigma_{1}^{2}}-\frac{1}{\sigma_{2}^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial^{2}}{\partial l^{2}}\ln\frac{p_{2}(l)}{p_{1}(l)}=\frac{1}{\sigma_{1}^{2}}-\frac{1}{\sigma_{2}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Concentration Case (<math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}^{2}&gt;\sigma_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}^{2}&gt;\sigma_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> The second derivative is negative, indicating that <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{*}=\frac{\sigma_{1}^{2}\mu_{2}-\sigma_{2}^{2}\mu_{1}}{\sigma_{1}^{2}-\sigma_{2}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{*}=\frac{\sigma_{1}^{2}\mu_{2}-\sigma_{2}^{2}\mu_{1}}{\sigma_{1}^{2}-\sigma_{2}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a unique <span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">maximum point</span>. In LLM reasoning, this is the most common scenario: while incorrect trajectories vary significantly (lengthy loops or abrupt failures), correct trajectories tend to concentrate within a specific logical complexity. The policy is thus encouraged to stay within this “reliable” length zone.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dispersion Case (<math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}^{2}&lt;\sigma_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}^{2}&lt;\sigma_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{*}=\frac{\sigma_{1}^{2}\mu_{2}-\sigma_{2}^{2}\mu_{1}}{\sigma_{1}^{2}-\sigma_{2}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{*}=\frac{\sigma_{1}^{2}\mu_{2}-\sigma_{2}^{2}\mu_{1}}{\sigma_{1}^{2}-\sigma_{2}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> becomes a <span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">minimum point</span>. This implies that the correctness probability is higher at extreme lengths (very short or very long) and lowest at <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. For variable stability, we clip these cases to the observed boundaries in our implementation.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Degenerate Case (<math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}^{2}=\sigma_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}^{2}=\sigma_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> Due to the randomness of parameter estimation, this is an almost impossible scenario. However, for the sake of rigor, we discuss this scenario in detail below.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Analysis of the Degenerate Case (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}^{2}=\sigma_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}^{2}=\sigma_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>).</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Although the exact equality <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}=\sigma_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}=\sigma_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is unlikely in practice with sampled data, it represents a critical theoretical threshold where the curvature of the log-probability ratio vanishes. When variances are identical, the quadratic terms in the exponent of the Gaussian distributions cancel out:</p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(l)=\ln\frac{p_{2}(l)}{p_{1}(l)}=\frac{1}{2\sigma^{2}}\left[(l-\mu_{1})^{2}-(l-\mu_{2})^{2}\right]+C=\frac{\mu_{2}-\mu_{1}}{\sigma^{2}}l+C^{\prime}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(l)=\ln\frac{p_{2}(l)}{p_{1}(l)}=\frac{1}{2\sigma^{2}}\left[(l-\mu_{1})^{2}-(l-\mu_{2})^{2}\right]+C=\frac{\mu_{2}-\mu_{1}}{\sigma^{2}}l+C^{\prime},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are constants independent of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, the relationship between length and correctness becomes <span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">strictly monotonic</span>:</p>
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1}&gt;\mu_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1}&gt;\mu_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the slope is negative, implying that every additional token strictly decreases the likelihood of success. This suggests that the model should adopt a “minimalist” strategy (<math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\text{opt}}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mtext>opt</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\text{opt}}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1}&lt;\mu_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1}&lt;\mu_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the slope is positive, suggesting that accuracy is directly proportional to reasoning length, pushing the optimal target to be as long as possible (<math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\text{opt}}\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mtext>opt</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\text{opt}}\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1}=\mu_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1}=\mu_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}^{2}=\sigma_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}^{2}=\sigma_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(l)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(l)</annotation></semantics></math> is constant, meaning length provides no information about correctness.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">This linear degradation highlights the importance of the variance term in our theorem. When <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}^{2}&gt;\sigma_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}^{2}&gt;\sigma_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the variance difference provides the “repelling force” that creates a stable, finite peak for the optimal length, preventing the model from collapsing into trivial (zero length) or infinitely redundant outputs.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Geometric Interpretation of the Shift.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The optimal length can be rewritten as a biased estimate of the mean of correct trajectories:</p>
<table id="A1.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\text{opt}}=\mu_{2}+\underbrace{\frac{\sigma_{2}^{2}}{\sigma_{1}^{2}-\sigma_{2}^{2}}(\mu_{2}-\mu_{1})}_{\text{Correction Bias}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mtext>opt</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Correction Bias</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\text{opt}}=\mu_{2}+\underbrace{\frac{\sigma_{2}^{2}}{\sigma_{1}^{2}-\sigma_{2}^{2}}(\mu_{2}-\mu_{1})}_{\text{Correction Bias}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This decomposition reveals how the disparity between correct and total samples shifts the target:</p>
<ul id="A1.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{2}&lt;\mu_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{2}&lt;\mu_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> (correct samples are shorter on average), the correction bias is negative. Thus, <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\text{opt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>l</mi><mtext>opt</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\text{opt}}</annotation></semantics></math> will be <span id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">smaller</span> than the mean correct length <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. This mathematically justifies a “strict efficiency” penalty, where the model is pushed to be even more concise than the current average success.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The term <math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sigma_{2}^{2}}{\sigma_{1}^{2}-\sigma_{2}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sigma_{2}^{2}}{\sigma_{1}^{2}-\sigma_{2}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> acts as a “variance leverage”. If the correct trajectories are highly consistent (<math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{2}^{2}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{2}^{2}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>), then <math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\text{opt}}\approx\mu_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mtext>opt</mtext></msup><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\text{opt}}\approx\mu_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, relying directly on the empirical success mean.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Summary of Parameter Relationships.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A1.T4" title='Table 4 ‣ Summary of Parameter Relationships. ‣ A.2 In-depth Analysis of the Optimal Length 𝑙^"opt" ‣ Appendix A Math Supplement ‣ SmartThinker: Progressive Chain-of-Thought Length Calibration for Efficient Large Language Model Reasoning' class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 4</span></a> summarizes the theoretical behavior of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> under different statistical conditions.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="A1.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Behavior of <math id="A1.T4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\text{opt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>l</mi><mtext>opt</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\text{opt}}</annotation></semantics></math> under different <math id="A1.T4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.T4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> conditions.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A1.T4.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A1.T4.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T4.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A1.T4.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Condition</span></th>
<th id="A1.T4.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A1.T4.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Mathematical Property</span></th>
<th id="A1.T4.5.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A1.T4.5.1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Reasoning Intuition</span></th>
<th id="A1.T4.5.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="A1.T4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\text{opt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">l</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">opt</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\text{opt}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.T4.5.1.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> Strategy</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A1.T4.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T4.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><math id="A1.T4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}^{2}&gt;\sigma_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">&gt;</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}^{2}&gt;\sigma_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T4.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="A1.T4.5.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Local Maximum</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="A1.T4.5.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Existence of a ”Golden Length”</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="A1.T4.5.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Computed <math id="A1.T4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\text{opt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>l</mi><mtext>opt</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\text{opt}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T4.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A1.T4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}^{2}=\sigma_{2}^{2},\mu_{1}&gt;\mu_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">μ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">&gt;</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">μ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}^{2}=\sigma_{2}^{2},\mu_{1}&gt;\mu_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T4.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A1.T4.5.3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Linear Decrease</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A1.T4.5.3.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Shorter is strictly better</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left"><math id="A1.T4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.T4.5.3.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> (min length)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T4.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A1.T4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}^{2}=\sigma_{2}^{2},\mu_{1}&lt;\mu_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">μ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">μ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}^{2}=\sigma_{2}^{2},\mu_{1}&lt;\mu_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T4.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A1.T4.5.4.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Linear Increase</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A1.T4.5.4.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Complexity aids accuracy</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left"><math id="A1.T4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.T4.5.4.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> (max length)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T4.5.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb"><math id="A1.T4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}^{2}&lt;\sigma_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}^{2}&lt;\sigma_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T4.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><span id="A1.T4.5.5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Local Minimum</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><span id="A1.T4.5.5.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Unstable middle-ground</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><span id="A1.T4.5.5.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0 (boundary clipping)</span></td></tr>
